#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186114979 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ce2e21aa-f89d-5d10-b815-c66a2b46ef5c" :knowledge-point/title "Representing a 2x2 System of Equations Using a Matrix Product"}] :question/id #uuid "87bf279f-9f78-54cb-b9c3-e1bf1c5426ff" :question/math-academy-id "e-4505" :question/problem "Represent the following system of equations using matrices:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2x=5 \\\\ -5x+6y=-8\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's write the system so that both $x$ and $y$ appear in each equation. The variable $y$ does not appear in the first equation, but this just means its coefficient is $0.$ So, we get\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2x+0y=5 \\\\ -5x+6y=-8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $A\\mathbf{x} = \\mathbf{b},$ where\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 6\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -8\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $A\\mathbf{x} = \\mathbf{b}$ becomes\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 6\\end{aligned}]\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186114980 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f4f746a1-ea9e-5136-90d6-d4dee1306c17" :knowledge-point/title "Representing a 2x2 System of Equations Using a Matrix Product by Reorganizing"}] :question/id #uuid "359f4b72-60d2-54e2-b7ef-c48f1e3af708" :question/math-academy-id "e-4506" :question/problem "Represent the following system of equations using matrices:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}-5y=-3x \\\\ 6+x=-2+y\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we organize the system so that it’s in the correct order:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}3x-5y=0 \\\\ x-y=-8.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $A\\mathbf{x} = \\mathbf{b},$ where\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}3 & -5 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -8\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $A\\mathbf{x} = \\mathbf{b}$ becomes\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}3 & -5 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186114981 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fe2300a1-f31e-5a24-889a-6f45e1e8647b" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing a Matrix Product as a 2x2 System of Equations"}] :question/id #uuid "b87aa5eb-f689-5f34-baeb-f97c3f200552" :question/math-academy-id "e-4507" :question/problem "What is the system of equations represented by\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}10 & -15 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The  $2\\times 2$ matrix represents the coefficients of $x$ and $y,$ while the $2\\times 1$ column vector on the right-hand side represents the constants of the equations. So, we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}10x-15y=5 \\\\ 1x+0y=-2\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimplifying both equations in the system, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}2x-3y=1 \\\\ x=-2.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186285546 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f4f746a1-ea9e-5136-90d6-d4dee1306c17" :knowledge-point/title "Representing a 2x2 System of Equations Using a Matrix Product by Reorganizing"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "81b5a246-ca9e-5135-a33d-50d686162fa2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285548} {:answer/id #uuid "501e4add-5935-5574-bcdd-8185631cdcda" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285549} {:answer/id #uuid "38a2bf1e-62e2-5828-b7e0-58e1eb72e89f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 & -4 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285550} {:answer/id #uuid "963953c3-2de9-59df-bc09-eb191c32a73a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285551} {:answer/id #uuid "341ac451-2f52-5d83-ba21-84040d7b347e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}4 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285552}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "501e4add-5935-5574-bcdd-8185631cdcda" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285549} :answer-field/id #uuid "99bcc160-6b29-52b3-824c-53a118bbf9d2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285547}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "653bbc46-49d8-5a42-a29a-f56c9b28ffda" :question/math-academy-id "q-130510" :question/problem "Represent the following system of equations using matrices:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}3x-1=4y \\\\ y=-4\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we organize the system so that it’s in the correct order and  both $x$ and $y$ appear in each equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}3x-4y=1 \\\\ 0x+y=-4\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\nb=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $Ax=b$ becomes\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}3 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}].\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186285553 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f4f746a1-ea9e-5136-90d6-d4dee1306c17" :knowledge-point/title "Representing a 2x2 System of Equations Using a Matrix Product by Reorganizing"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "015102c4-80c9-58b1-a6f7-19c738d6ae83" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & -5 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285555} {:answer/id #uuid "5ffaa568-3aa2-5a0c-b90f-1b6c7d74887c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285556} {:answer/id #uuid "666bb6ce-8c69-58bb-9f64-c074a586ea60" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & -5 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285557} {:answer/id #uuid "912f023c-8f3b-5869-a11a-adf430077540" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & -5 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285558} {:answer/id #uuid "d7a8be72-9a44-5ab4-b506-2cc4e732ec0b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285559}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d7a8be72-9a44-5ab4-b506-2cc4e732ec0b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285559} :answer-field/id #uuid "3bb0b38f-8f80-5d8f-849c-717575f90366" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285554}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f1e0ebea-fd8e-5d3c-88fb-b9fe91d02ab3" :question/math-academy-id "q-130511" :question/problem "Represent the following system of equations using matrices:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}x-5=y \\\\ y=2x+3\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we organize the system so that it’s in the correct order and  both $x$ and $y$ appear in each equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}x-y=5 \\\\ -2x+y=3\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\nb=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $Ax=b$ becomes\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186285560 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f4f746a1-ea9e-5136-90d6-d4dee1306c17" :knowledge-point/title "Representing a 2x2 System of Equations Using a Matrix Product by Reorganizing"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dfa8a3c1-1953-5b60-90d6-3f12f8a0559f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285562} {:answer/id #uuid "7ef42529-a50f-5611-a0c0-3026ef319cc2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285563} {:answer/id #uuid "3ee76527-3857-5fdb-a8b8-3120a2ba7f1c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285564} {:answer/id #uuid "cc812d9e-40c9-59b3-966d-992276b8fef9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285565} {:answer/id #uuid "75abb477-0847-5cdb-9775-bb1ad7d67e38" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285566}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7ef42529-a50f-5611-a0c0-3026ef319cc2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285563} :answer-field/id #uuid "db39cf70-312a-5626-9516-1869e70f97dc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285561}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b00f7b70-6dac-5214-a6e4-7e29ea035240" :question/math-academy-id "q-130514" :question/problem "Represent the following system of equations using matrices:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}-3=y \\\\ 1=-2+x\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we organize the system so that it’s in the correct order and  both $x$ and $y$ appear in each equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}0x+y=-3 \\\\ x+0y=3\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\nb=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $Ax=b$ becomes\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186285567 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fe2300a1-f31e-5a24-889a-6f45e1e8647b" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing a Matrix Product as a 2x2 System of Equations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dcc7b819-d34d-5e43-95c9-c1b281f2d4c9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}10x+25y=-15 \\\\ 12x+3y=6\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285569} {:answer/id #uuid "9dc182d2-9706-5763-93dc-587dab323cb4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}2x+5y=3 \\\\ 4x+y=-2\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285570} {:answer/id #uuid "623abe45-ff87-5e43-9dc1-245c2962faf2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}10x+5y=-15 \\\\ 12x+3y=6\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285571} {:answer/id #uuid "baa1cfed-e269-547a-9c12-2e3d7b76faa5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}10x+25y=-15 \\\\ 12x+6y=3\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285572} {:answer/id #uuid "5674977b-88eb-5d70-9612-43da6db8de1b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}2x+5y=15 \\\\ 4x+y=-6\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285573}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9dc182d2-9706-5763-93dc-587dab323cb4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}2x+5y=3 \\\\ 4x+y=-2\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285570} :answer-field/id #uuid "d80dc95a-ccfe-5c63-add0-c28ed2aa747c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285568}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7dad4c0b-b40d-5232-bf24-f4b25c943bdf" :question/math-academy-id "q-130523" :question/problem "What is the system of equations represented by\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}10 & 25 \\\\ 12 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}15 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}]?\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The  $2\\times 2$ matrix represents the coefficients of $x$ and $y,$ while the $2\\times 1$ column vector on the right-hand side represents the constants of the equations. So, we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}10x+25y=15 \\\\ 12x+3y=-6\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimplifying both equations in the system, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}2x+5y=3 \\\\ 4x+y=-2.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186285574 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fe2300a1-f31e-5a24-889a-6f45e1e8647b" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing a Matrix Product as a 2x2 System of Equations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "52009efc-6824-563a-8800-e47b7b7fb1bf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}3x-4y=3 \\\\ x=-1\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285576} {:answer/id #uuid "d89a6c2b-c6fe-5d74-8e38-057a628b3cdc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}3x-4y=-1 \\\\ x=3\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285577} {:answer/id #uuid "3c8fbc81-1587-564a-9d92-83d4d8974ebd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}3y-4x=-1 \\\\ y=3\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285578} {:answer/id #uuid "fb656ae0-aa0e-5ecd-8bc6-794d55dcef2a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}3x-4y=-1 \\\\ y=3\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285579} {:answer/id #uuid "1a79b223-c6dd-528c-b8c8-c31a562b85cd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}3x-4y=-3 \\\\ y=1\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285580}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fb656ae0-aa0e-5ecd-8bc6-794d55dcef2a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}3x-4y=-1 \\\\ y=3\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285579} :answer-field/id #uuid "05885c37-6ceb-521d-949d-ae7bce94f247" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285575}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d89fd9f8-ce5b-5e2b-ac3f-e1b0b0d325d3" :question/math-academy-id "q-130525" :question/problem "What is the system of equations represented by\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}3 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]?\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The  $2\\times 2$ matrix represents the coefficients of $x$ and $y,$ while the $2\\times 1$ column vector on the right-hand side represents the constants of the equations. So, we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}3x-4y=-1 \\\\ 0x+y=3\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimplifying both equations in the system, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}3x-4y=-1 \\\\ y=3.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186285581 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fe2300a1-f31e-5a24-889a-6f45e1e8647b" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing a Matrix Product as a 2x2 System of Equations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "20e38e88-d080-5cb1-b4b4-8dbcd026e8ce" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}5y=9 \\\\ x=-1\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285583} {:answer/id #uuid "4b868c55-527f-5f22-8286-e5009a6a81e2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}5y=9 \\\\ x=1\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285584} {:answer/id #uuid "125a0777-46eb-594d-8249-3dc124ce15af" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}5y=-9 \\\\ x=-1\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285585} {:answer/id #uuid "926e048d-aef3-5568-b093-c2dcab326665" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}x+5y=9 \\\\ x=-1\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285586} {:answer/id #uuid "efb011e8-139d-58bc-8d8a-66ec60112b01" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}x+5y=9 \\\\ y=-1\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285587}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "20e38e88-d080-5cb1-b4b4-8dbcd026e8ce" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}5y=9 \\\\ x=-1\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285583} :answer-field/id #uuid "f96113ad-9483-5c89-8541-d3e70ab96e7d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285582}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a1162f6f-3b06-5edc-926f-fe3ac4ca244f" :question/math-academy-id "q-130528" :question/problem "What is the system of equations represented by\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}0 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]?\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The  $2\\times 2$ matrix represents the coefficients of $x$ and $y,$ while the $2\\times 1$ column vector on the right-hand side represents the constants of the equations. So, we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}0x+5y=9 \\\\ x+0y=-1\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimplifying both equations in the system, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}5y=9 \\\\ x=-1.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186285588 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ce2e21aa-f89d-5d10-b815-c66a2b46ef5c" :knowledge-point/title "Representing a 2x2 System of Equations Using a Matrix Product"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "599c5dbe-2277-5ee8-9ecd-fe7b44c6e710" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285590} {:answer/id #uuid "2d2302a5-eff9-5c31-b72a-7dd8a8fa236f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285591}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2d2302a5-eff9-5c31-b72a-7dd8a8fa236f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285591} :answer-field/id #uuid "f4dc1ef5-2662-5f63-a853-840f3483d67c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285589} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dbae3307-7c77-5e2e-9fd4-bf714bdb23fe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285593}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dbae3307-7c77-5e2e-9fd4-bf714bdb23fe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285593} :answer-field/id #uuid "c334698a-43f2-563f-ac8f-04678c6af2b5" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285592} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b9a8cea3-295b-5c15-a14b-457c0ad8f15e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285595}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b9a8cea3-295b-5c15-a14b-457c0ad8f15e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285595} :answer-field/id #uuid "6ef273dd-4559-50d8-bd92-6a2d6c8c9ea2" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285594} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f5c77894-a8d5-5d24-a2c1-0a164d86301c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285597}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f5c77894-a8d5-5d24-a2c1-0a164d86301c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285597} :answer-field/id #uuid "cc9e1340-0139-5002-b0b9-c4d02e1bb0a3" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285596}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7d57abb8-94fa-56f9-8d2a-a453c16c2648" :question/math-academy-id "q-317494" :question/problem "For the following system of equations\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}-3x+4y=10 \\\\ 5x+2y=-7,\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nits representation using matrices is\n\n| |  | {{field-1}} | $4$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-2}} | {{field-3}} |  | |  |  |  | |  | $x$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $y$ |  | | $=$ | |  | {{field-4}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $-7$ |  | |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-1}} | $4$ |  |  |  |  |\n|  | {{field-2}} | {{field-3}} |  |  |  |  |\n|  | $x$ |  |  |  |  |  |\n|  | $y$ |  |  |  |  |  |\n|  | {{field-4}} |  |  |  |  |  |\n|  | $-7$ |  |  |  |  |  |\n\n." :question/worked-solution "First, notice that both $x$ and $y$ appear in each equation, all the variables are on the left-hand side, and all the constants are on the right-hand side.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}-3x+4y=10 \\\\ 5x+2y=-7\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 4 \\\\ 5 & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\nb=[\\begin{aligned}10 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $Ax=b$ becomes\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 4 \\\\ 5 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}10 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}].\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186285598 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ce2e21aa-f89d-5d10-b815-c66a2b46ef5c" :knowledge-point/title "Representing a 2x2 System of Equations Using a Matrix Product"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f3596704-6fa8-58b1-8392-a250a5444f76" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285600}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f3596704-6fa8-58b1-8392-a250a5444f76" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285600} :answer-field/id #uuid "731a984d-b95d-5c89-a685-22b9784d90ae" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285599} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "feb45f9c-11e8-562c-94ca-719f9001fe66" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285602}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "feb45f9c-11e8-562c-94ca-719f9001fe66" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285602} :answer-field/id #uuid "f415aea3-5475-5682-a17a-0b5011c5410b" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285601} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b50707b5-4c9e-550d-a2ac-776967ac9fec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285604}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b50707b5-4c9e-550d-a2ac-776967ac9fec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285604} :answer-field/id #uuid "e1b4898b-0011-51e7-bc96-841a173d3dbc" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285603} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f12c772c-b0c5-594f-8b5f-57f2dd4259cf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285606}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f12c772c-b0c5-594f-8b5f-57f2dd4259cf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285606} :answer-field/id #uuid "21b222cb-0f2d-588b-b05d-c5289a4f997b" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285605}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "bfa79505-f094-536b-8de1-28d863aaf777" :question/math-academy-id "q-317500" :question/problem "For the following system of equations\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}-6y=4 \\\\ 3x+5y\\,=-7\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nits representation using matrices is\n\n| |  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-3}} | $5$ |  | |  |  |  | |  | $x$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $y$ |  | | $=$ | |  | $4$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-4}} |  | |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} |  |  |  |  |\n|  | {{field-3}} | $5$ |  |  |  |  |\n|  | $x$ |  |  |  |  |  |\n|  | $y$ |  |  |  |  |  |\n|  | $4$ |  |  |  |  |  |\n|  | {{field-4}} |  |  |  |  |  |\n\n." :question/worked-solution "First, let's write the system so that both $x$ and $y$ appear in each equation. \nThe variable $x$ does not appear in the first equation, but this just means its coefficient is $0.$ So, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}0x-6y=4 \\\\ 3x+5y\\,=-7\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -6 \\\\ 3 & 5\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\nb=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $Ax=b$ becomes\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}0 & -6 \\\\ 3 & 5\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}].\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186285607 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ce2e21aa-f89d-5d10-b815-c66a2b46ef5c" :knowledge-point/title "Representing a 2x2 System of Equations Using a Matrix Product"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "65eb3fcd-89b6-50d1-8030-8e0e856b8493" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285609} {:answer/id #uuid "7eb2804d-566e-5894-9673-8e2e5f70f0d8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285610}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "65eb3fcd-89b6-50d1-8030-8e0e856b8493" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285609} :answer-field/id #uuid "9b657339-550d-5381-ae3f-5e005e506ec4" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285608} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "98c12c81-cbcd-5d39-ac3d-a523d98124ea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285612}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "98c12c81-cbcd-5d39-ac3d-a523d98124ea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285612} :answer-field/id #uuid "8b9df299-3855-56ba-9143-e274a7d7fb31" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285611} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2dd4d4fa-c097-55f2-9bb3-97cf9ef0b37b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285614}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2dd4d4fa-c097-55f2-9bb3-97cf9ef0b37b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285614} :answer-field/id #uuid "4c1c2edf-0660-5cef-90b2-8f6f60c0eb7f" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285613} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5cbf5118-38a1-5913-9c1f-50e22b2d244c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285616}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5cbf5118-38a1-5913-9c1f-50e22b2d244c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285616} :answer-field/id #uuid "f19887aa-a43c-5431-8dde-6e40e1cb03ed" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285615}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "af3e197c-8649-56f3-9c21-c51a5293b5c1" :question/math-academy-id "q-317506" :question/problem "For the following system of equations\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}-5x=10 \\\\ 4y=-12\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nits representation using matrices is\n\n| |  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-3}} | $4$ |  | |  |  |  | |  | $x$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $y$ |  | | $=$ | |  | $10$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-4}} |  | |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} |  |  |  |  |\n|  | {{field-3}} | $4$ |  |  |  |  |\n|  | $x$ |  |  |  |  |  |\n|  | $y$ |  |  |  |  |  |\n|  | $10$ |  |  |  |  |  |\n|  | {{field-4}} |  |  |  |  |  |\n\n." :question/worked-solution "First, let's write the system so that both $x$ and $y$ appear in each equation. The variable $y$ does not appear in the first equation, but this just means its coefficient is $0.$ Similarly, the variable $x$ does not appear in the second equation, which means that its coefficient is $0$ too. \n\nSo, we get\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-5x+0y=10 \\\\ 0x+4y=-12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\nb=[\\begin{aligned}10 \\\\ -12\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $Ax=b$ becomes\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}10 \\\\ -12\\end{aligned}].\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186285617 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ce2e21aa-f89d-5d10-b815-c66a2b46ef5c" :knowledge-point/title "Representing a 2x2 System of Equations Using a Matrix Product"}] :question/answer-fie