ue "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285635}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d8a1a7a8-8ef2-5197-971b-6eabce3e744a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285635} :answer-field/id #uuid "1d5f2876-4f24-5a66-91ea-9e515e40bfaf" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285634}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1ecd543f-2212-556d-8aa1-795c0b79c684" :question/math-academy-id "q-317521" :question/problem "For the following system of equations\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}2x+5=y \\\\ 3x-2y=7,\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nits representation using matrices is\n\n| |  | {{field-1}} | $-1$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-2}} | {{field-3}} |  | |  |  |  | |  | $x$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $y$ |  | | $=$ | |  | {{field-4}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $7$ |  | |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-1}} | $-1$ |  |  |  |  |\n|  | {{field-2}} | {{field-3}} |  |  |  |  |\n|  | $x$ |  |  |  |  |  |\n|  | $y$ |  |  |  |  |  |\n|  | {{field-4}} |  |  |  |  |  |\n|  | $7$ |  |  |  |  |  |\n\n." :question/worked-solution "First, we organize the system so that it is in the correct order and  both $x$ and $y$ appear in each equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}2x-y=-5 \\\\ 3x-2y=7\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\nb=[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $Ax=b$ becomes\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}].\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186285636 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f4f746a1-ea9e-5136-90d6-d4dee1306c17" :knowledge-point/title "Representing a 2x2 System of Equations Using a Matrix Product by Reorganizing"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f9c343a1-d172-5942-8b4a-e0759aa92444" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285638}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f9c343a1-d172-5942-8b4a-e0759aa92444" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285638} :answer-field/id #uuid "e7e45197-bbc4-522c-9bbf-eabdba33f705" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285637} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0e3d4d50-f411-58ef-9647-6592215b18f3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285640}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0e3d4d50-f411-58ef-9647-6592215b18f3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285640} :answer-field/id #uuid "31d3dddc-5cdf-5458-b65d-64ce63b5e305" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285639} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "25fce9dd-4418-571a-8006-fb53dba401f7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285642}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "25fce9dd-4418-571a-8006-fb53dba401f7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285642} :answer-field/id #uuid "b4ee6fe0-01ce-5e92-9eb6-9df772c5c188" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285641} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0bb1773c-6b74-5e2b-be8e-083c224ac9f0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285644}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0bb1773c-6b74-5e2b-be8e-083c224ac9f0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285644} :answer-field/id #uuid "5c5af3c7-6c7b-5c54-9f0d-bf82d4af0887" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285643}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "837cc9d4-4e9c-5181-aa72-7d095c6ebf76" :question/math-academy-id "q-317530" :question/problem "For the following system of equations\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}y-2x=9 \\\\ -5y\\,=-15,\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nits representation using matrices is\n\n| |  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-3}} | $-5$ |  | |  |  |  | |  | $x$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $y$ |  | | $=$ | |  | $9$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-4}} |  | |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} |  |  |  |  |\n|  | {{field-3}} | $-5$ |  |  |  |  |\n|  | $x$ |  |  |  |  |  |\n|  | $y$ |  |  |  |  |  |\n|  | $9$ |  |  |  |  |  |\n|  | {{field-4}} |  |  |  |  |  |\n\n." :question/worked-solution "First, we organize the system so that it is in the correct order and both $x$ and $y$ appear in each equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}-2x+y=9 \\\\ 0x-5y=-15\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -5\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\nb=[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ -15\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $Ax=b$ becomes\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -5\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ -15\\end{aligned}].\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186285645 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fe2300a1-f31e-5a24-889a-6f45e1e8647b" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing a Matrix Product as a 2x2 System of Equations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a344c21a-7262-57b3-b539-d28a39877f9f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285647}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a344c21a-7262-57b3-b539-d28a39877f9f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285647} :answer-field/id #uuid "7d18fa30-0a01-5cda-993c-23471879166d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285646} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "40dc865d-421c-54e7-9c3f-a44e856600da" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285649}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "40dc865d-421c-54e7-9c3f-a44e856600da" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285649} :answer-field/id #uuid "f77d43a0-806e-58d5-983d-4cc667a1304b" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285648}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1966b892-d016-52e7-ab33-ef1036c65c29" :question/math-academy-id "q-317582" :question/problem "What is the system of equations represented by\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}]?\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system of equations is\n\n| { | {{field-1}} | $=$ | $5$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| {{field-2}} | $=$ | $\\,\\,-7.$ |  |" :question/worked-solution "The  $2\\times 2$ matrix represents the coefficients of $x$ and $y,$ while the $2\\times 1$ column vector on the right-hand side represents the constants of the equations. So, we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}0x+1y=5 \\\\ -1x+0y=-7\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimplifying both equations in the system, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}y=5 \\\\ -x=-7\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115652 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fe2300a1-f31e-5a24-889a-6f45e1e8647b" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing a Matrix Product as a 2x2 System of Equations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ddf0cd7f-e5e4-5843-9832-6ff022f43e14" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{2x - 5y = 10; x =-7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113313} {:answer/id #uuid "02f87275-1680-5e69-b30f-e34823497555" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{2x + 5y =-7; x = 10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113314} {:answer/id #uuid "36ec4f5e-d9de-58bf-88e1-fb9f8dc1838e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{2x - 5y =-7; x = 10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113315} {:answer/id #uuid "4c68845b-874c-5896-9f16-ac96d40fe1b8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{2x + 5y = 10; y =-7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113316} {:answer/id #uuid "4f327003-eb35-5ffb-a303-754812dc5872" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{2x - 5y = 10; y =-7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113317}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ddf0cd7f-e5e4-5843-9832-6ff022f43e14" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{2x - 5y = 10; x =-7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113313} :answer-field/id #uuid "83377318-ace5-5f3b-836e-6b1faff567b5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113312}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d80073fa-9f5d-593f-a765-d5bf9c3d142b" :question/math-academy-id "q-31876" :question/problem "What is the system of equations represented by\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}2 & -5 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}10 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}]?\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The  $2\\times 2$ matrix represents the coefficients of $x$ and $y,$ while the $2\\times 1$ column vector on the right-hand side represents the constants of the equations. So, we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}2x-5y=10 \\\\ x+0y=-7\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimplifying both equations in the system, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}2x-5y=10 \\\\ x=-7\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186285650 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ce2e21aa-f89d-5d10-b815-c66a2b46ef5c" :knowledge-point/title "Representing a 2x2 System of Equations Using a Matrix Product"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "47197821-619f-51a6-82ce-d54af2eaea13" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}6 & 4 \\\\ 1 & -8\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285652} {:answer/id #uuid "9c7e4a87-0ccf-5442-9394-6d6198430eba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}4 & 6 \\\\ 1 & -8\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285653} {:answer/id #uuid "3afeeea5-c70f-5c0e-9980-611df72a772e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}6 & 4 \\\\ -8 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285654} {:answer/id #uuid "91c08ead-41cd-519d-8f35-1e709aa6a9ec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}6 & 4 \\\\ 1 & -8\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285655} {:answer/id #uuid "1dedcf90-45e9-517f-9e62-c066a769067d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}6 & 1 \\\\ 4 & -8\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285656}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "91c08ead-41cd-519d-8f35-1e709aa6a9ec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}6 & 4 \\\\ 1 & -8\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285655} :answer-field/id #uuid "3af624a1-47e6-52b7-a769-b3beea42cdfc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285651}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0847a4d1-d888-5fc9-a642-ee058523fb86" :question/math-academy-id "q-8820" :question/problem "Represent the following system of equations using matrices:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}6x+4y=1 \\\\ x-8y=-2\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that both $x$ and $y$ appear in each equation, all the variables are on the left-hand side, and all the constants are on the right-hand side.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}6x+4y=1 \\\\ x-8y=-2\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}6 & 4 \\\\ 1 & -8\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\nb=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $Ax=b$ becomes\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}6 & 4 \\\\ 1 & -8\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$"}]}
